<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tusheti</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tusheti is a remote mountain region of north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a> on the northern slopes of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greater-caucasus">Greater Caucasus</a>, bordering <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chechnya">Chechnya</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dagestan">Dagestan</a>. Its people, the Tush, lived from sheep herding, moving their flocks between summer pastures and the lowlands of Kakheti, and built fortified villages with defensive towers. The Tush served as warriors of the kings of Kakheti.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tusheti.jpg" alt="Tusheti" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Alex Maisuradze · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Keselo,_Tusheti.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
